    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64070" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῠκάνθρωπ-ος</span></b> , ὁ and
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>were-wolf</i> or <i>man-wolf</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Marc.Sid.
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> s. h. v.) ap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.719
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				6.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.16
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῠκανθρωπ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, a kind of
			madness, <i>in which the patient had the ravenous appetite and
				other qualities of a wolf</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				<u>Syn.</u>
				8.9
			</span></i>.</div>
